# Data conversion between tebibyte and terabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between tebibyte and terabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1TiB to 1.0995TB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5TiB yields 1.6492TB; backward, converting 1TB to 0.9094TiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5TB yields 1.3642TiB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1TiB
print(forward_whole->to(TB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TiB
print(forward_fractional->to(TB))
backward_whole: int = 1TB
print(backward_whole->to(TiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TB
print(backward_fractional->to(TiB))

<<< stdout
1.0995TB
1.6492TB
0.9094TiB
1.3642TiB

<<< stderr
